WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.865
A drone operations center turns individual flights into a governed program.

00:00:06.865 --> 00:00:17.574
It coordinates mission intake, approval, roles, scheduling, aircraft, payloads, live support, data products, safety, privacy, security, and compliance.

00:00:17.574 --> 00:00:25.538
Strong governance defines purpose, scope, authority, exclusions, handoffs, escalation, and pilot command responsibility.

00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:35.149
Facilities and systems should support secure storage, battery safety, planning, communication, maintenance, data protection, and recovery.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:45.309
Scheduling combines current airspace, weather, location, crew readiness, aircraft status, payload fit, emergency options, and data requirements.

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:52.723
Fleet management tracks each asset, battery, configuration, defect, repair, and lifecycle decision.

00:00:52.723 --> 00:01:03.433
Live support prioritizes safety information, clear communication, action-oriented status, emergency coordination, and decision logging without replacing the pilot.

00:01:03.433 --> 00:01:10.297
Data workflows preserve provenance, metadata, originals, privacy, confidence, and specialist review.

00:01:10.297 --> 00:01:18.810
The goal is reliable, safe, lawful, privacy-conscious, and accountable operation, not simply more flights.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:30.618
Continuous improvement comes from maintenance evidence, after-action review, audit trails, and a culture willing to pause unsafe or unjustified missions.
